namespace Ponca
{
/*!
 \page fittingreference Fitting module: reference

 \tableofcontents

 This page lists what the Fitting module provides: fitting procedures, computational objects and their capabilities,
 derivatives, neighbor filters, weight kernels, status codes and factory entries. The usage of these classes is
 explained in the \ref fitting.

 \section fittingreference_primitiveoverview Fitting procedures

 The fitting procedures approximate the neighborhood by a geometric primitive. They are used as the first
 computational objects of a Ponca::Basket, e.g. `Basket<Point, Filter, OrientedSphereFit>`.

 | Procedure                               | Primitive              | Input                         | Dim. | Signed | CUDA | References |
 |-----------------------------------------|------------------------|-------------------------------|------|--------|------|------------|
 | Ponca::CovariancePlaneFit               | Ponca::Plane           | positions                     | any  | no     | yes  | \cite Pauly:2002:PSSimplification |
 | Ponca::MeanPlaneFit                     | Ponca::Plane           | positions and normals         | any  | yes    | yes  | |
 | Ponca::CovarianceLineFit                | Ponca::Line            | positions                     | any  | no     | yes  | |
 | Ponca::SphereFit                        | Ponca::AlgebraicSphere | positions                     | any  | no     | no   | \cite Guennebaud:2007:APSS |
 | Ponca::OrientedSphereFit                | Ponca::AlgebraicSphere | positions and normals         | any  | yes    | yes  | \cite Guennebaud:2007:APSS |
 | Ponca::UnorientedSphereFit              | Ponca::AlgebraicSphere | positions and unoriented normals | any | no  | no   | \cite Chen:2013:NOMG |
 | Ponca::MongePatchQuadraticFit           | Ponca::MongePatch      | positions                     | 3    | no     | no   | \cite Cazals:2005:Jets |
 | Ponca::MongePatchRestrictedQuadraticFit | Ponca::MongePatch      | positions                     | 3    | no     | no   | \cite Cazals:2005:Jets |

 - *Signed*: value of `fit.isSigned()`. When `false`, the orientation of the scalar field (and of its gradient) is
   arbitrary: only its zero isosurface and the direction of its gradient are meaningful.
 - *CUDA*: the procedure can be used in CUDA kernels (see \ref ponca_gpu_page).
 - Ponca::CovariancePlaneFit is `CovariancePlaneFitImpl<CovarianceBase<MeanPosition<Plane>>>`, and similarly for the
   other aliases; the `*Impl` classes can be used to build custom arrangements (see \ref fitting_multiprimitive).
 - The scalar field of a primitive (its *potential*) is: the signed distance for Ponca::Plane, the squared distance
   for Ponca::Line, the algebraic distance \f$u_c + \mathbf{u}_l^T\mathbf{x} + u_q\mathbf{x}^T\mathbf{x}\f$ for
   Ponca::AlgebraicSphere, and the difference \f$h(u,v) - h\f$ between the height field and the height of the point
   for Ponca::MongePatch.

 Ponca::CNC is not a fitting procedure of a basket, but a compute object of its own, see \ref fitting_curvature.

 \section fittingreference_tools Other computational objects

 | Class                                          | Computes                                                                 | Requires |
 |------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|
 | Ponca::DryFit                                  | nothing (counts the neighbors; mostly useful for testing and benchmarks)  | |
 | Ponca::MeanPosition                            | weighted barycenter of the neighbors                                     | |
 | Ponca::MeanNormal                              | weighted mean of the normals                                             | points with normals |
 | Ponca::CovarianceBase                          | covariance of the positions, its eigen decomposition and derived features | Ponca::MeanPosition |
 | Ponca::GLSParam                                | Growing Least Squares parameters \f$\tau, \eta, \kappa\f$ \cite Mellado:2012:GLS | an algebraic sphere |
 | Ponca::QuadraticHeightField, Ponca::RestrictedQuadraticHeightField | height field \f$h(u, v)\f$ over the tangent plane    | 3D, Ponca::HeightField |
 | Ponca::FundamentalFormWeingartenEstimator     | first and second fundamental forms, Weingarten map                       | a Monge patch (3D) |
 | Ponca::NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator    | Weingarten map from the spatial derivatives of the normal (BasketDiff)   | 3D, space derivatives |
 | Ponca::WeingartenCurvatureEstimator, Ponca::WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer | principal curvatures and directions from a Weingarten map | 3D, a Weingarten map and a tangent plane basis |

 \section fittingreference_outputandcapabilities Capabilities

 Computational objects are described by the capabilities they provide, expressed as C++20 concepts defined in
 `Ponca/src/Fitting/concepts.h`. Each capability gives access to a cast function, which returns the basket seen as the
 class providing the capability, and guarantees that a set of functions is available:

 | Capability (concept)                        | Cast function           | Main functions                                                         | Provided by |
 |---------------------------------------------|-------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
 | Ponca::ProvidesProjectionOperator           | `projectionOperator()`  | `project(q)`                                                           | Ponca::Plane, Ponca::Line, Ponca::AlgebraicSphere, Ponca::MongePatch |
 | Ponca::ProvidesImplicitPrimitive            | `implicitPrimitive()`   | `potential()`, `potential(q)`, `primitiveGradient()`, `primitiveGradient(q)`, `changeBasis(newCenter)`, and the projection | Ponca::Plane, Ponca::Line, Ponca::AlgebraicSphere, Ponca::MongePatch |
 | Ponca::ProvidesPlane                        | `plane()`               | `setPlane(normal, position)`, and the API of `Eigen::Hyperplane` (`normal()`, `offset()`, ...) | Ponca::Plane |
 | Ponca::ProvidesLine                         | `line()`                | `setLine(origin, direction)`, and the API of `Eigen::ParametrizedLine` (`origin()`, `direction()`, ...) | Ponca::Line |
 | Ponca::ProvidesAlgebraicSphere              | `algebraicSphere()`     | `uc()`, `ul()`, `uq()`, `center()`, `radius()`, `isPlane()`, `prattNorm()`, `prattNorm2()`, `applyPrattNorm()`, `isNormalized()`, `isValid()`, `isApprox(other, eps)` | Ponca::AlgebraicSphere |
 | Ponca::ProvidesMeanPosition                 | `meanPosition()`        | `barycenter()`, `barycenterDistance()`                                 | Ponca::MeanPosition |
 | Ponca::ProvidesMeanNormal                   | `meanNormal()`          | `meanNormalVector()`                                                   | Ponca::MeanNormal |
 | Ponca::ProvidesPositionCovariance           | `covarianceBase()`      | `solver()`, `lambda_0()`, `lambda_1()`, `lambda_2()`, `surfaceVariation()`, `planarity()`, `linearity()`, `sphericity()`, `anisotropy()`, `eigenentropy()` | Ponca::CovarianceBase |
 | Ponca::ProvidesTangentPlaneBasis            | `tangentPlaneBasis()`   | `worldToTangentPlane(q, isPositionVector)`, `tangentPlaneToWorld(q, isPositionVector)` | Ponca::CovariancePlaneFitImpl, Ponca::NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator |
 | Ponca::ProvidesGLSParam                     | `glsParam()`            | `tau()`, `eta()`, `kappa()`, `tau_normalized()`, `eta_normalized()`, `kappa_normalized()`, `fitness()`, `compareTo(other, useFitness)` | Ponca::GLSParam |
 | Ponca::ProvidesHeightFieldBase              | `heightFieldBase()`     | access to the height and the \f$(u, v)\f$ coordinates of a local vector | Ponca::HeightField |
 | Ponca::ProvidesHeightField                  | `heightField()`         | `height(u, v)`, `h_uu()`, `h_vv()`, `h_uv()`, `h_c()`, `dh_du(u, v)`, `dh_dv(u, v)`, `d2h_duu(u, v)`, `d2h_dvv(u, v)`, `d2h_duv(u, v)` | Ponca::QuadraticHeightField, Ponca::RestrictedQuadraticHeightField |
 | Ponca::ProvidesMongePatch                   | `mongePatchPrimitive()` | the implicit primitive of the patch                                    | Ponca::MongePatch |
 | Ponca::ProvidesFirstFondamentalFormComponents, Ponca::ProvidesSecondFondamentalFormComponents | `firstFondamentalFormComponent()`, `secondFondamentalFormComponent()` | `firstFundamentalFormComponents(E, F, G)`, `secondFundamentalFormComponents(L, M, N)` | Ponca::MongePatch |
 | Ponca::ProvidesWeingartenMap                | (none)                  | `weingartenMap()`, `weingartenMap(W)`                                  | Ponca::FundamentalFormWeingartenEstimator, Ponca::NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator |
 | Ponca::ProvidesMeanCurvature                | `meanCurvature()`       | `kMean()`                                                              | Ponca::AlgebraicSphere, Ponca::WeingartenCurvatureEstimator, Ponca::WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer, Ponca::CNC |
 | Ponca::ProvidesPrincipalCurvatures          | `curvatureTensor()`     | `kmin()`, `kmax()`, `kminDirection()`, `kmaxDirection()`, `GaussianCurvature()`, `kMean()` | Ponca::WeingartenCurvatureEstimator, Ponca::WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer, Ponca::CNC |

 Notes on the outputs:
 - Ponca::AlgebraicSphere::kMean() returns \f$2u_q\f$, which is the mean curvature only when the sphere is normalized
   (see `applyPrattNorm()`); Ponca::GLSParam::kappa() applies the normalization.
 - Ponca::GLSParam::eta() returns the gradient of the scalar field at the evaluation position, which is a unit vector
   only on the fitted surface of a normalized sphere.
 - `surfaceVariation()` returns \f$d\,\lambda_0 / \sum_i \lambda_i\f$, where \f$d\f$ is the dimension and
   \f$\lambda_0 \leq \lambda_1 \leq \dots\f$ the eigenvalues of the covariance; `planarity()`, `linearity()` and
   `sphericity()` are only valid in 3D \cite Guinard:2017.
 - Ponca::CovariancePlaneFitImpl::worldToTangentPlane returns the coordinates \f$(h, u, v)\f$ of a vector in the
   basis formed by the normal (first) and the tangent directions of the plane, relatively to the evaluation position;
   Ponca::CovariancePlaneFitImpl::tangentPlaneToWorld is its inverse.

 \section fittingreference_derivatives Derivatives

 The following classes are used in a Ponca::BasketDiff (see \ref fitting_derivatives). Derivatives are stored with the
 layout described in \ref fitting_derivatives_layout.

 | Capability (concept)                         | Cast function            | Main functions                         | Provided by |
 |----------------------------------------------|--------------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------|
 | Ponca::ProvidesImplicitPrimitiveDerivative   | `implicitPrimitiveDer()` | `dPotential()`, `dNormal()`            | Ponca::CovariancePlaneDer (3D), Ponca::OrientedSphereDer, Ponca::UnorientedSphereDer, Ponca::MlsSphereFitDer |
 | Ponca::ProvidesMeanPositionDerivative        | `meanPositionDer()`      | `barycenterDerivatives()`              | Ponca::MeanPositionDer |
 | Ponca::ProvidesMeanNormalDer                 | `meanNormalDer()`        | `dMeanNormal()`                        | Ponca::MeanNormalDer |
 | Ponca::ProvidesPositionCovarianceDer         | `covarianceDer()`        | derivatives of the covariance (internal) | Ponca::CovarianceDer |
 | Ponca::ProvidesCovariancePlaneDer            | `covariancePlaneDer()`   | `dPotential()`, `dNormal()`            | Ponca::CovariancePlaneDer |
 | Ponca::ProvidesGeomVar                       | `geomVar()`              | `geomVar(wtau, weta, wkappa)`          | Ponca::GLSDer (scale derivatives) |
 | (GLS derivatives)                            | `glsDer()`               | `dtau()`, `deta()`, `dkappa()`, `dtau_normalized()`, `deta_normalized()`, `dkappa_normalized()` | Ponca::GLSDer |

 Ponca::OrientedSphereDer and Ponca::UnorientedSphereDer also provide `algebraicSphereDer()`, and the derivatives of
 the parameters of the sphere (`m_dUc`, `m_dUl`, `m_dUq`).

 \section fittingreference_curvature Curvature estimators

 | Estimator                         | Type definition                                                              | Quantities |
 |-----------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------|
 | Surface variation, PCA distance   | `Basket<P, F, CovariancePlaneFit>`                                           | `surfaceVariation()`, `potential()` |
 | Growing Least Squares             | `Basket<P, F, OrientedSphereFit, GLSParam>`                                  | `kappa()`  |
 | PCA normal derivatives            | `BasketDiff<Basket<P, F, CovariancePlaneFit>, FitSpaceDer, CovariancePlaneDer, NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator, WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer>` | tensor |
 | Monge patches                     | `Basket<P, F, MongePatchQuadraticFit>`, `Basket<P, F, MongePatchRestrictedQuadraticFit>` | tensor |
 | APSS                              | `BasketDiff<Basket<P, F, OrientedSphereFit>, FitSpaceDer, OrientedSphereDer, NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator, WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer>` | tensor |
 | ASO                               | `BasketDiff<Basket<P, F, OrientedSphereFit>, FitSpaceDer, OrientedSphereDer, MlsSphereFitDer, NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator, WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer>` | tensor |
 | CNC                               | `CNC<P, UniformGeneration>`, `CNC<P, IndependentGeneration>`, `CNC<P, HexagramGeneration>`, `CNC<P, AvgHexagramGeneration>` | tensor |

 "Tensor" stands for the capability Ponca::ProvidesPrincipalCurvatures. Their usage, sign conventions and references
 are given in \ref fitting_curvature_page.

 \section fitting_filters Neighbor filters

 | Class                                                        | Construction                         | Frame      | Weight of \f$\mathbf{q}\f$ | `evalScale()` |
 |--------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|------------|----------------------------|---------------|
 | Ponca::DistWeightFilter<DataPoint, WeightKernel>             | `{p, t}` or `{point, t}`             | centered   | \f$\phi(\|\mathbf{q}-\mathbf{p}\|/t)\f$, 0 beyond \f$t\f$ for compact kernels | \f$t\f$ |
 | Ponca::NoWeightFilter<DataPoint>                             | `{p}` (a scale is accepted and ignored) | centered | 1                          | 1             |
 | Ponca::NoWeightFilterGlobal<DataPoint>                       | default (parameters are ignored)     | global     | 1                          | 1             |
 | Ponca::FilterWithAttributes<DataPoint, DataType, Filter, Converter> | `{p, t, data}` or `{point, t}` (then `data = Converter(point)`) | as `Filter` | as `Filter` | as `Filter` |

 - Ponca::DistWeightFilter assumes \f$t > 0\f$ (this is not checked).
 - The derivatives of the weight (`scaledw`, `spacedw`, ...) are computed from the derivatives of the kernel for
   Ponca::DistWeightFilter, and are null for the other filters.
 - Ponca::FilterWithAttributes stores an additional attribute, available with `data()`. Ponca::CNC uses it to store
   the normal of the evaluation point, with a Ponca::DistWeightFilter and a constant kernel.

 \section fitting_kernel Weight kernels

 Ponca::DistWeightFilter weights a neighbor at distance \f$d\f$ from the evaluation position by \f$\phi(x)\f$, with
 \f$x = d/t\f$, where \f$p\f$ is the evaluation location and \f$t\f$ the scale:

 | Class                                          | \f$\phi(x)\f$                                         | Compact | `df` | `ddf` | Notes |
 |------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|---------|------|-------|-------|
 | Ponca::ConstantWeightKernel<Scalar>            | \f$c\f$ (1 by default, see `setValue`)                 | yes     | yes  | yes   | uniform weights in the ball |
 | Ponca::SmoothWeightKernel<Scalar>              | \f$(x^2-1)^2\f$                                        | yes     | yes  | yes   | default choice |
 | Ponca::PolynomialSmoothWeightKernel<Scalar, m, n> | \f$(x^n-1)^m\f$                                     | yes     | yes  | yes   | negative on \f$[0,1)\f$ for odd \f$m\f$; in the current version, `df` is only exact for \f$n = 2\f$ |
 | Ponca::WendlandWeightKernel<Scalar>            | \f$(1-x)^4(4x+1)\f$                                    | yes     | yes  | yes   | \cite Alexa:2009:Hermite |
 | Ponca::SingularWeightKernel<Scalar>            | \f$1/x^2\f$                                            | yes     | yes  | yes   | infinite at \f$x = 0\f$: the evaluation position must not coincide with a point |
 | Ponca::CompactExpWeightKernel<Scalar>          | \f$\exp\left(\frac{-x^2}{1-x^2}\right)\f$              | yes     | yes  | no    | \f$C^\infty\f$ |
 | Ponca::GaussianWeightKernel<Scalar>            | \f$\exp\left(-\frac{x^2}{2}\right)\f$                  | no      | yes  | yes   | standard deviation \f$t\f$; \f$\phi(1) \approx 0.6\f$ |

 *Compact* kernels vanish for \f$x \geq 1\f$: Ponca::DistWeightFilter then gives a null weight to the points farther
 than \f$t\f$. The columns `df` and `ddf` tell whether the first and second derivatives are valid (flags `isDValid`
 and `isDDValid`), which is required to compute first and second order derivatives of the fits.

 \section fittingreference_status Fit status

 The status codes are described in \ref fitting_Checkstatus. They are set as follows:

 | Class                                         | Rule |
 |-----------------------------------------------|------|
 | Ponca::BasketUnitBase (all baskets)           | Ponca::UNDEFINED when no neighbor has a positive weight, Ponca::STABLE otherwise |
 | Ponca::CovarianceBase                         | Ponca::UNDEFINED with fewer than `Dim` neighbors, or when the eigen decomposition fails |
 | Ponca::SphereFit, Ponca::OrientedSphereFit, Ponca::UnorientedSphereFit | Ponca::UNDEFINED with fewer than `Dim` neighbors, Ponca::UNSTABLE with fewer than \f$2\times\f$`Dim` neighbors |
 | Ponca::OrientedSphereFit                      | Ponca::UNDEFINED when the weighted spread of the positions vanishes (e.g. all the neighbors at the same position) |
 | Ponca::MongePatchQuadraticFit, Ponca::MongePatchRestrictedQuadraticFit | Ponca::NEED_OTHER_PASS after the first pass if the plane is stable, then Ponca::STABLE |
 | Ponca::CNC                                    | Ponca::UNDEFINED when no neighbor lies in the ball or when the total area of the triangles is null |
 | All fitting procedures                        | Ponca::CONFLICT_ERROR_FOUND when their primitive has already been computed by another class |

 Derivative extensions return the status of the basket they differentiate.

 \section fittingreference_schemes Evaluation schemes and projection operators

 | Class                                         | Description |
 |-----------------------------------------------|-------------|
 | Ponca::SingleEvaluationScheme                 | performs a single fit |
 | Ponca::MLSEvaluationScheme<Scalar>            | iterates fits and projections until convergence (MLS projection), see \ref evaluation_schemes |
 | Ponca::DirectProjectionOperator               | projection given by the primitive (`project`) |
 | Ponca::GradientDescentProjectionOperator      | moves the point along the gradient of the scalar field (16 steps by default) |

 \section fittingreference_factory Factory entries

 Ponca::Factory<Point, Filter, DiffType> lists the following compute objects, retrieved by name with
 `GetMethod<"name">()` (see \ref fitting_factory):

 | Name                              | Compute object                                                      | Availability |
 |-----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------|
 | `DryFit`                          | `Basket<P, NF, DryFit>`                                             | all          |
 | `MeanPosition`                    | `Basket<P, NF, MeanPosition>`                                       | all          |
 | `MeanNormal`                      | `Basket<P, NF, MeanNormal>`                                         | all          |
 | `CovarianceLineFit`               | `Basket<P, NF, CovarianceLineFit>`                                  | all          |
 | `CovariancePlaneFit`              | `Basket<P, NF, CovariancePlaneFit>`                                 | all          |
 | `SphereFit`                       | `Basket<P, NF, SphereFit>`                                          | all          |
 | `MeanPlaneFit`                    | `Basket<P, NF, MeanPlaneFit>`                                       | all          |
 | `APSS`                            | `Basket<P, NF, OrientedSphereFit, GLSParam>`                        | all          |
 | `UnorientedAPSS`                  | `Basket<P, NF, UnorientedSphereFit, GLSParam>`                      | all, except with nvcc |
 | `MongePatchQuadratic`             | `Basket<P, NF, MongePatchQuadraticFit>`                             | 3D           |
 | `MongePatchRestrictedQuadratic`   | `Basket<P, NF, MongePatchRestrictedQuadraticFit>`                   | 3D           |
 | `CNCUniform`, `CNCIndependent`, `CNCHexagram`, `CNCAvgHexagram` | `CNC<P, UniformGeneration>`, ...      | 3D           |
 | `ASO`                             | `BasketDiff<Basket<P, NF, OrientedSphereFit, GLSParam>, DiffType, OrientedSphereDer, MlsSphereFitDer, NormalDerivativeWeingartenEstimator, WeingartenCurvatureEstimatorDer>` | 3D, `DiffType` containing Ponca::FitSpaceDer |

 Note that the CNC entries ignore the neighbor filter type `NF`: they use their own filter. The predicates available
 to filter the lists are `XXXProvider` and `NotXXXProvider` for `XXX` in: `Derivatives`, `ProjectionOperator`,
 `ImplicitPrimitive`, `AlgebraicSphere`, `MeanPosition`, `MeanNormal`, `GLSParam`, `GeomVar`, `Plane`, `Line`,
 `HeightField`, `MongePatch`, `PositionCovariance`, `PrincipalCurvatures`, `TangentPlaneBasis` and `MeanCurvature`
 (the corresponding concepts are named `ProvidesXXX`).
 */
} // namespace Ponca
